<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Harris, 1st Baron Harris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1746–1829</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as General George Harris</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Harris, 1st Baron Harris (1746–1829), was a British army officer who served in the American War of Independence, where he was wounded at Bunker Hill. As commander-in-chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> army he led the British and Hyderabadi forces that invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-anglo-mysore-war">Fourth Anglo-Mysore War</a> and stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> in May 1799, ending the rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>. He was made a baron in 1815.</p></div>
